# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values. Never commit .env.local.

# Supabase project (Project Settings -> API)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Gemini API key, free tier (aistudio.google.com/apikey -> Create API key).
# Server-only — no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, so it's never sent to the browser.
# Required for "Giao việc" (task assignment) on the CEO Command Center to work.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional text fallback providers — only used when Gemini's free quota runs
# out AND the agent has no direct reports (delegating agents stay
# Gemini-only, see agent-runner.ts). Tried in this order: DeepSeek, Grok,
# OpenAI. Leave any of these blank to skip that provider entirely — nothing
# breaks, Gemini-only behavior is unchanged. Get keys from
# platform.deepseek.com, console.x.ai, and platform.openai.com respectively
# (each is a separate paid account, not the same as GEMINI_API_KEY).
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
GROK_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the model used for each fallback provider, in case the
# defaults in text-fallback.ts (unverified — this project can't reach these
# APIs to test live) get rejected as "model not found".
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat
# GROK_MODEL=grok-4
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Optional: override the Gemini model used for real image generation (only
# agents flagged agents.image_generation = true use this — see migration
# 0013 and agent-runner.ts). Uses the SAME GEMINI_API_KEY above — free tier,
# no extra account. Unverified model name — override here if it 404s.
# GEMINI_IMAGE_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-image

# Optional: read-only bridge into AME29 Nail's SEPARATE Firebase app
# (ame29-nail.netlify.app — real bookings + revenue, not part of this
# project). Only used by agents flagged can_read_schedule/can_read_revenue
# (see migration 0014). Value is the ENTIRE content of the Firebase service
# account JSON file (Firebase Console -> Project settings -> Service
# accounts -> Generate new private key), pasted as one value — paste it
# directly into Vercel's Environment Variables, never into chat or a
# committed file. This key can read AND write everything in that Firebase
# project (Firestore Rules don't apply to it) — src/lib/firebase-admin.ts
# only ever calls .get(), never .set()/.update()/.delete()/.add(), but that
# discipline lives in this project's code, not in the key's own permissions.
# If you want Google to enforce read-only at the key level too, create a
# separate service account with only the "Cloud Datastore Viewer" IAM role
# instead of the default one.
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY=

# Required only for the daily Google Maps auto-sync cron
# (src/app/api/cron/sync-competitors/route.ts) — NOT needed for the
# competitors admin page itself, which uses the normal user-session client.
# Supabase Project Settings -> API -> "service_role" key (NOT the anon key —
# this one bypasses Row Level Security entirely). Server-only, never expose
# to the browser, never commit.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Shared secret the cron route checks against Vercel's own
# `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET` header (Vercel adds this
# automatically to every scheduled request once this var is set) — stops
# anyone else from hitting the endpoint and burning your Google Places
# quota. Any random string works; generate one with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
CRON_SECRET=

# Optional: Telegram push notifications when a top-level "Giao việc" task
# finishes, fails, or needs approval, and for the daily auto business report
# (see src/lib/telegram.ts). Leave both blank to skip — nothing breaks, the
# dashboard result display works exactly the same either way.
# 1. Chat with @BotFather on Telegram -> /newbot -> pick any name -> it
#    replies with a token (looks like 123456:ABC-DEF...) -> that's below.
# 2. Send that new bot any message (it can't message you first), then open
#    https://api.telegram.org/bot<YOUR_TOKEN>/getUpdates in a browser and
#    find the number at "chat":{"id": ...} -> that's TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# Optional: Google Places API (New) key, for automatically refreshing
# Google Maps rating/review_count once a day for any competitor row that has
# a google_place_id set (see src/lib/google-places.ts). Get one at
# console.cloud.google.com -> APIs & Services -> Credentials, with the
# "Places API (New)" enabled — free tier covers this project's volume
# (a few dozen place lookups a day). Leave blank to skip auto-sync entirely;
# the competitors admin page still works, you just update Google Maps
# numbers by hand like everything else.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# Required for the AME29 Content OS ingestion pipeline
# (src/app/api/cron/process-inbox/route.ts) — watches the "00 INBOX" folder
# in Google Drive, classifies new photos/videos with Gemini, and auto-files
# them into the right category/month folder (or "99 REVIEW" when unsure).
# See README.md for the full Drive folder setup.
#
# Value is the ENTIRE content of a Google Cloud Service Account JSON key
# file, pasted as one value:
# 1. console.cloud.google.com -> create/select a project -> enable the
#    "Google Drive API".
# 2. IAM & Admin -> Service Accounts -> Create Service Account (any name,
#    no roles needed — access is granted via Drive sharing, not IAM).
# 3. Open the new service account -> Keys -> Add Key -> Create new key ->
#    JSON -> downloads a .json file.
# 4. Paste that file's entire content here (or directly into Vercel's
#    Environment Variables) — never into chat or a committed file.
# 5. In Google Drive, share the "AME29 PHOTO LIBRARY" root folder with the
#    service account's email (looks like
#    xxx@yyy.iam.gserviceaccount.com, found inside the JSON as
#    "client_email") as Editor. Works with a regular personal Gmail Drive —
#    no Google Workspace required.
# 6. Set business_units.google_drive_root_folder_id (Supabase Table Editor)
#    to that root folder's ID (the long string in its Drive URL after
#    /folders/).
GOOGLE_DRIVE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY=

# Required for real Facebook Page / Instagram Business posting + tracking
# (Kênh MXH page, src/app/api/social/**, src/lib/social/facebook.ts,
# src/lib/social/instagram.ts). Both platforms share ONE Meta app.
# 1. developers.facebook.com -> My Apps -> Create App -> type "Business".
# 2. Add product "Facebook Login for Business" (App settings -> add product).
# 3. App settings -> Basic: copy "App ID" (FACEBOOK_APP_ID below) and "App
#    Secret" (FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET below, click Show first).
# 4. Facebook Login for Business -> Settings: add this exact Valid OAuth
#    Redirect URI (must match NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL below exactly):
#    https://<your-site>/api/social/callback/facebook
# 5. App Review -> Permissions and Features: request
#    pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement, pages_manage_posts,
#    instagram_basic, instagram_content_publish, instagram_manage_insights.
#    Each needs a short screen-recording demo + why it's used — Meta's
#    review can take several days. Until approved, the app only works for
#    accounts added as Admin/Developer/Tester under App Roles (fine for
#    testing with your own Page).
# 6. The Facebook Page needs an Instagram Business/Creator account linked
#    to it (Page Settings -> Linked accounts) for Instagram posting to
#    work at all — a personal IG account won't work.
FACEBOOK_APP_ID=
FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET=

# Required for real TikTok posting + tracking (src/lib/social/tiktok.ts).
# 1. developers.tiktok.com -> Manage apps -> Create an app.
# 2. Add product "Content Posting API" (Login Kit is added automatically).
# 3. App details page: copy "Client key" (TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY) and "Client
#    secret" (TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET).
# 4. Login Kit -> Redirect URI: add exactly
#    https://<your-site>/api/social/callback/tiktok
# 5. Content Posting API -> request scopes user.info.basic, video.publish,
#    video.list. An unaudited app can only post as SELF_ONLY (private,
#    visible only to the account that posted it) to accounts you add as
#    Target users under the app — TikTok requires a demo video + audit
#    before public posting works for real, which can take 1-2 weeks.
# 6. Once TikTok approves public posting, set TIKTOK_PRIVACY_LEVEL below
#    (e.g. PUBLIC_TO_EVERYONE) — leave blank until then, it defaults to
#    the safe SELF_ONLY so nothing posts publicly by accident.
TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=
TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=
# TIKTOK_PRIVACY_LEVEL=SELF_ONLY

# Public base URL this app is served from — must match EXACTLY what's
# registered as the OAuth redirect URI in both the Meta and TikTok apps
# above (including https://, no trailing slash). Defaults to the current
# Netlify URL if left blank (see src/lib/site-url.ts) — only needs setting
# here if the site later moves to a different domain.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://tnt-corporate-o.netlify.app
